#
#	riscv32-specific files
#
# Every other architecture here hand-writes memset/memmove/strchr in
# native assembly; za has none yet, so these use the generic portable
# C fallbacks (memset.c/memmove.c/strchr.c) instead of an riscv32
# version of the assembly ones -- correct, just not the fastest
# instruction sequence QEMU's cores could run.
TARGFILES=\
	vlop-riscv32.$O\
	vlrt-riscv32.$O\
	memset.$O\
	memmove.$O\
	strchr.$O\
